  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Pretty much just as the title says. Proximity is obviously broken on some objects that have triggers on them. Changing the proximity value seems to do absolutely nothing. This was originally reported back in October 2018 (https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/pickup-proximity-value-does-not-work-properly) and was marked as under review but nothing seemed to have come of it. In fact, it seems worse now. My maps that I created never used to do this until only a month or two ago. Someone on that canny post, @Bryan Bortz (I have no idea how to tag people sorry) also reported that it's gotten worse only recently which matches up with what I've found as well.\n\nHere's an example of what I'm talking about. This is a decently big map I've created, and I can quite literally hit one of my triggers from across the entire map. Changing the proximity values of the trigger does nothing. This screenshot was taken with triggers on the default settings (Proximity 2).\n\nOne thing that's interesting to note is it's not all objects that do this. I have a cube for example just across from all of those drills off in the distance that I'm able to target, but only when I'm very close to it. They both use the same proximity settings though.",
